# Feature Delivery — session safety (FDA-001 v1.5)

Non-negotiable rules during Feature Delivery sessions. Full workflow: [`.cursor/skills/feature-delivery/SKILL.md`](../skills/feature-delivery/SKILL.md). Charter: [`docs/dev/feature-delivery-agent.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery-agent.mdoc). Branch protocol: [`docs/dev/feature-delivery/branch-and-data-preservation.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/branch-and-data-preservation.mdoc). Design/research: [`docs/dev/feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc).

## Git, branch, and WIP (mandatory)

- **Never** change branch, create a worktree, or run forbidden git ops during a Feature Delivery session unless the **current user task** explicitly authorizes that **exact** operation.
- At **D0**: write `.cache/feature-delivery/<sessionId>/branch-checkpoint.json` — see branch-and-data-preservation §1.
- Lock the **actual** starting branch as `lockedBranch`; verify `git branch --show-current` at every checkpoint ([SC-GIT-01](stop-conditions)).
- `initialHead` is baseline evidence only; `currentHead` may advance after authorized commits on `lockedBranch`.
- **Never** modify, revert, stash, restore, clean, or reset unrelated user WIP. Wrong direction → STOP report + pivot memo, not auto-revert.
- Forbidden without unlock: `checkout`, `switch`, `merge`, `rebase`, `reset`, `clean`, `restore`, `stash`, force-push ([SC-GIT-05](stop-conditions)–[SC-GIT-06](stop-conditions)).
- Feature branch creation requires explicit user contract: exact name, source branch/SHA, creation intent ([SC-GIT-07](stop-conditions)).
- Before **every** commit: emit `BRANCH_CHECKPOINT_PRE_COMMIT`. Before **every** push: emit `BRANCH_CHECKPOINT_PRE_PUSH` — branch-and-data-preservation §7.
- Parallel Cursor chats on same local workspace → **SHARED_WORKSPACE_BRANCH_RISK** ([SC-WORKSPACE-01](stop-conditions)).
- Committed data not visible on current branch is **not** lost — read-only `git log --all`, `branch --contains`, `reflog`, `fsck` before claiming deletion ([SC-DATA-05](stop-conditions)).
- Prefer **hard-stop + clear report** over continuing on uncertain branch.

## Discovery and design (D0–D7)

- **No source implementation** before mandatory D-stages for session tier — [staged-design-workflow.mdoc](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/staged-design-workflow.mdoc).
- **Do not code after a basic plan** — complete D0–D7 (tier-dependent) first.
- D0 baseline + branch checkpoint → D1 requirements matrix → D2 consumer map → D3 data contract → D4 architecture → D5 UI/UX → D6 test realness → D7 failure modes.
- **Workflow tiers:** A UI-only reduced; B API/DB full; C platform/finance/notification/tenant deepest.
- CP1 legacy = D5 + D1; doc-first on protected paths unchanged.
- **pnpm workspace only** — never NX or `nx affected`.
- Stub/route/seed/read-only catalog ≠ complete feature.

## Planning and scope

- **Do not implement** before approved CP1 design + CP2 plan.
- Stage and commit only files within `scopePaths` (+ allowed `docs/**` when doc-first applies).
- Scope expansion beyond approved plan → hard-stop.

## Architecture

- **architecture-reviewer** mandatory for platform candidates and multi-consumer primitives — [`.cursor/agents/architecture-reviewer.md`](../agents/architecture-reviewer.md).
- Keyword / classifier signals are **not** architecture decisions.
- Preserve workspace-agnostic shared primitives (WAC-001).
- Preserve **Denali / Urban / starter** divergence.
- **No Big Bang refactor** in a feature session.
- Notification/inbox: [`notification-case-study.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/notification-case-study.mdoc) — module-specific multi-consumer → **SC-ARCH-02**.

## Research and UI/UX

- Internet research when official behavior, accessibility, security, UX placement, or unclear blockers warrant it — record in `research.json`; never override repo constraints or hard stops.
- **Mandatory UI/UX gate (CP1):** for every **user-visible** feature, produce `ui-ux-decision.json` (24 sections) before source implementation — [research-and-design-gate §3.3](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/research-and-design-gate.mdoc).
- **UI UX Pro Max** is **advisory only** — use when skill + `python3` available per [FDA-INTEGRATION](../skills/ui-ux-pro-max/FDA-INTEGRATION.md); fallback checklist when unavailable; never claim Pro Max used without ledger row.
- **Priority:** product requirements → repository tokens/primitives → Denali/Urban/starter → accessibility/RTL/LTR → Pro Max recommendations.
- **UI/UX gate (CP5) + BQC:** inspect existing placement; real browser proof; RTL/LTR; all states; screenshots/traces; [Playwright best practices](https://playwright.dev/docs/best-practices).
- curl/API/build **never** equals `ui-browser-verified`. Unavailable browser → `ui-unverified` or `ui-accepted-risk`, not PASS.

## Adversarial bug-hunt (B1–B8)

After implementation — [adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/adversarial-bug-hunt.mdoc):

- B1 static → B2 contract → B3 RLS → B4 integration → B5 browser (BQC) → B6 resilience → B7 regression → B8 independent second review.
- Per finding: reproduce → root cause → smallest fix → regression test → rerun → re-check relevant D-stage.
- **Forbidden:** UI symptom fix when root cause is API/contract/persistence/auth.
- Skipped B-pass for tier → `unverified`; blocks `FEATURE_COMPLETE`.

## Verification and evidence

- **No claim without ledger evidence** — [`evidence-ledger-schema.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/evidence-ledger-schema.mdoc).
- **SKIP ≠ PASS.** Skipped checks → `UNVERIFIED`; never `COMPLETE`.
- Fast-track per [`tiered-testing.md`](../../docs/dev/tiered-testing.md); heavy gates need explicit user **YES**.
- Never hide failed tests or claim pass without ledger row.

## Blocker recovery (mandatory)

Per [`blocker-recovery.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/blocker-recovery.mdoc):

- **Never stop on first failure** — 11-step loop; up to **3 evidence-based hypotheses** before STOP.
- Classify: code, test, dependency, environment/browser/runtime, architecture, security/product.
- Recoverable: inspect source, adjacent implementations, scripts/env, repo docs, focused web research, smallest fix, narrowest rerun, ledger, resume queue.
- **Hard stops unchanged:** security/tenant/RLS, migration rewrite, production/secrets, unresolved product decisions — research never overrides.
- **Blocked sub-feature** must not stop unrelated queue items.
- Stop only when recovery exhausted or explicit human decision required.

## Full closure

Canonical rules: [`completion-rules.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/completion-rules.mdoc) (FDA-001 v1.5).

Verdicts: `FEATURE_COMPLETE` \| `FEATURE_COMPLETE_WITH_EXPLICIT_ACCEPTED_RISKS` \| `FEATURE_INCOMPLETE` \| `FEATURE_BLOCKED`

- Mandatory blocking statuses block `FEATURE_COMPLETE` — see completion-rules §2.
- Never emit `FEATURE_COMPLETE` when mandatory row is broken, missing, partial, or unverified.
- Accepted risks require explicit approval; never for security, RLS, tenant, durability, mandatory producers.
- Run `node .cursor/skills/feature-delivery/evaluate-fda-verdict.regression.mjs` before final verdict.

## Operations

- **No production/staging mutation** without explicit unlock ([SC-OPS-01](stop-conditions)).
- Doc-first on `packages/platform-core`, `packages/workspace-sdk`, `apps/api` — [`.cursorrules`](../../.cursorrules).

## Hard stop

If any condition in [`stop-conditions.mdoc`](../../docs/dev/feature-delivery/stop-conditions.mdoc) fires: **stop**, emit Feature Delivery STOP report with `stopId`, evidence, required decision. Do not continue on that path.

**Recoverable failures** → blocker-recovery first unless `BR-SEC` or `BR-PROD`.
